<title>ITALY: ITALY'S ROLO BANK STOCK SUSPENDED LIMIT UP.</title>
<headline>ITALY'S ROLO BANK STOCK SUSPENDED LIMIT UP.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in Italian bank Rolo Banca 1473 was suspended on the Milan bourse when the share price exceeded the 10 percent upside limit.</p>
<p>Dealers said the stock was suspended at a theoretical price of 22,500 lire after rising strongly in heavy volume all morning in line with other major banking shares.</p>
<p>Rolo had closed on Wednesday 2.64 percent lower, the stock neglected as the market generally rallied.</p>
<p>At 1332 GMT, the all-share Mibtel index was 2.56 percent up at 15,067 with gainers outnumbering losers by 189 to 47.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
